on-arrival: unions_timer = 3; month_actions += 1
frequency: 300
is-card: true
tags: movement

= The Trade Unions

Millions of workers belong to the Free Trade Unions, whose leaders back Ebert. The ultra-left says the unions are dead and must be replaced by revolutionary workers' unions; others say the party must go where the workers are.

- @inside: Work inside the existing unions.
- @outside: Build revolutionary unions outside them.
- @easy_discard

@inside
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs 10 Unity. ?] Wins workers and the USPD's respect; angers the ultra-left.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_name +] line forbids work inside the old unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_union_work == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 6;
Q.uspd_relation += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 10;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10;
!}

Communists stand in union elections and speak at every branch meeting. It is slow, unglamorous work.

@outside
subtitle: Pleases the ultra-left; splits the workforce.
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction += 10; unionist_satisfaction -= 10; worker_support += 2; militancy += 4

The new unions are small, militant and proud of it.
